# Security

Deny by default. Authenticate and authorize on the server for every sensitive operation. Do not trust document IDs, signer IDs, signature placement coordinates, or document state supplied by the browser; load authoritative state from persistence after authorization.

Never hardcode secrets, credentials, signing tokens, API keys, private URLs, or environment-specific values.

Treat uploaded documents, PDFs, images, headers, and client metadata as untrusted. Validate all external input at the system boundary with Zod (`packages/contracts`). Sanitize filenames and content types; do not execute or fetch from document content.

Public identifiers must be opaque (UUIDv7 or equivalent), never sequential. Store only hashes of signing bearer tokens, never the raw token. Use content-addressed or otherwise immutable object keys where practical.

Audit records are append-only; never update or delete them in application code. Use idempotency keys for mutation endpoints and retryable worker jobs.

Never log passwords, authorization headers, cookies, signing tokens, raw signatures, private document contents, or complete personal data. Log correlation IDs and opaque resource IDs only.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
logger.info('signer auth', { token: bearer, email, pdfBytes });

// ✅ GOOD
logger.info('signer session authorized', { correlationId, envelopeId, signerId });
```

Retryable work must be idempotent. Do not claim legal or compliance status from these controls alone.
